    whyItMatters: `Wrestling is widely regarded as one of the sport's most valuable base disciplines precisely because it lets a fighter choose where a fight takes place: a strong wrestler with a weaker ground game can still use takedowns purely to disrupt a dangerous striker, while a strong wrestler with a strong ground game can use the same skill to set up a finish.`,
