    howItWorks: `A fighter looking to break the clinch typically needs to first neutralise whatever control is being used against them, freeing a trapped arm, creating a frame with a forearm against the opponent's chest or head, or pushing off the cage, before actually stepping back to a safe striking distance. Breaking carelessly, simply shoving away without controlling the opponent's hands first, can expose a fighter to a clean strike the instant separation happens.`,
